{
  "$comment": [
    "Per-module coverage gates, expressed as data instead of as a chain of scripts.",
    "",
    "These groups were previously one `package.json` script per release",
    "(`test:v01216` ... `test:v01242`), each naming both its modules and its test",
    "files. That made the script list a second changelog and tied every coverage",
    "gate to a version number: renaming a module silently broke its gate, and",
    "adding one release meant another register-*.mjs script and another `&&` in the",
    "The same groups are defined here once.",
    "",
    "Each group runs as its own `node --test` invocation, exactly as before.",
    "Running all tests against every group in one process was measured to under-",
    "report some modules -- `context-retrieval-capture.ts` reads 98.67% lines that",
    "way but 100% in its own group -- so a single combined run would have turned",
    "this into a stricter gate than the one it replaces.",
    "",
    "Every managed group asserts 100% line, function, and branch coverage.",
    "Platform-only branches may remain explicitly skipped on platforms where they",
    "are structurally unreachable; no ordinary module is exempt from branch coverage."
  ],
  "thresholds": {
    "lines": 100,
    "functions": 100,
    "branches": 100
  },
